"""Story bank for the animated story Shorts (format since 05.11.2026).

Modelled on the "deen tales" style that goes viral on TikTok/Shorts: a short,
emotional everyday Muslim family story (struggle -> du'a / patience -> Allah's
answer) told in 3D-animation stills, closing with ONE verified reminder.

Rules (channel policy):
  * Characters are FICTIONAL everyday people. Never prophets, Sahaba or real
    persons, never a depiction of Allah, angels or the Kaaba interior.
  * Exactly one source per story, Qur'an or a famous sahih hadith, quoted
    faithfully (Sahih International wording, shortened only at clause ends).
  * Modest clothing; women in hijab; no music; no romance between non-mahram.
  * The characters TALK THEMSELVES (lip-synced): every scene has exactly one
    speaking character, framed as the biggest face (the shot says so). No
    narrator - the story is told through dialogue only.
  * ~120-150 spoken words, 9-12 scenes -> 45-65 s.

Schema per story:
  id, title (YouTube title), hook (first on-screen/spoken line),
  characters: {key: {"look": visual description, "voice": voice role}},
  setting: shared visual setting,
  scenes: [{"shot": image description, "lines": [[speaker, text], ...]}]
      speaker = a character key (one speaker per scene; "narrator" is legacy only)
  ending: {"arabic", "word", "reminder", "source"}  -> final card
  tags
"""

